From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Librescoot <hello@librescoot.org>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: let the first buffered write start playback

The hardware parameters set the start threshold to one period. Starting the
PCM immediately after prepare, while its buffer is still empty, guarantees an
underrun before QAudioSink's timer can provide the first period. Leave the PCM
prepared; ALSA starts it automatically once the first write reaches the
configured threshold. Once a finite pull source ends, do not query availability
on the drained PCM either: ALSA reports that completed stream as an xrun even
though it is the normal end-of-sample path.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/multimedia/alsa/qalsaaudiosink.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/multimedia/alsa/qalsaaudiosink.cpp b/src/multimedia/alsa/qalsaaudiosink.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/multimedia/alsa/qalsaaudiosink.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/alsa/qalsaaudiosink.cpp
@@ -347,7 +347,6 @@ bool QAlsaAudioSink::open()
     if(audioBuffer == 0)
         audioBuffer = new char[snd_pcm_frames_to_bytes(handle,buffer_frames)];
     snd_pcm_prepare( handle );
-    snd_pcm_start(handle);
 
     // Step 5: Setup timer
     bytesAvailable = bytesFree();
@@ -559,7 +558,7 @@ bool QAlsaAudioSink::deviceReady()
             // Did not get any data to output
             timer->stop();
             snd_pcm_drain(handle);
-            bytesAvailable = bytesFree();
+            bytesAvailable = buffer_size;
             if(bytesAvailable > snd_pcm_frames_to_bytes(handle, buffer_frames-period_frames)) {
                 // Underrun
                 if (deviceState != QAudio::IdleState) {
